"This node will be discretised by :class:`.Discretisation` and converted to "
"a :class:`pybamm.StateVector` node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/expression_tree/variable.rst:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/variable.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.variable.Variable:6
msgid ""
"name of the node domain : iterable of str, optional list of domains that "
"this variable is valid over"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/variable.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.variable.Variable:10
#: pybamm.expression_tree.variable.VariableDot:11
msgid ""
"dictionary of auxiliary domains ({'secondary': ..., 'tertiary': ..., "
"'quaternary': ...}). For example, for the single particle model, the "
"particle concentration would be a Variable with domain 'negative particle' "
"and secondary auxiliary domain 'current collector'. For the DFN, the "
"particle concentration would be a Variable with domain 'negative particle', "
"secondary domain 'negative electrode' and tertiary domain 'current collector'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/variable.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.variable.Variable:17
#: pybamm.expression_tree.variable.VariableDot:18
msgid ""
"A dictionary equivalent to {'primary': domain, auxiliary_domains}. Either "
"'domain' and 'auxiliary_domains', or just 'domains', should be provided (not "
"both). In future, the 'domain' and 'auxiliary_domains' arguments may be "
"deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/variable.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.variable.Variable:22
msgid "Physical bounds on the variable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/variable.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.variable.Variable:24
#: pybamm.expression_tree.variable.VariableDot:26
msgid ""
"The name to use for printing. Default is None, in which case self.name is "
"used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/variable.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.variable.Variable:26
#: pybamm.expression_tree.variable.VariableDot:28
msgid ""
"The scale of the variable, used for scaling the model when solving. The "
"state vector representing this variable will be multiplied by this scale. "
"Default is 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/variable.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.variable.Variable:30
#: pybamm.expression_tree.variable.VariableDot:32
msgid ""
"The reference value of the variable, used for scaling the model when "
"solving. This value will be added to the state vector representing this "
"variable. Default is 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/variable.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.variable.Variable:35
#: pybamm.expression_tree.variable.VariableDot:37
msgid "**Extends:** :class:`pybamm.expression_tree.variable.VariableBase`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/variable.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.variable.Variable.diff:1
#: pybamm.expression_tree.variable.VariableDot.diff:1
msgid ""
"Differentiate a symbol with respect to a variable. For any symbol that can "
"be differentiated, return `1` if differentiating with respect to yourself, "
"`self._diff(variable)` if `variable` is in the expression tree of the "
"symbol, and zero otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/variable.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.variable.Variable.diff:6
#: pybamm.expression_tree.variable.VariableDot.diff:6
msgid "The variable with respect to which to differentiate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/variable.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.variable.VariableDot:1
msgid ""
"A node in the expression tree represending the time derviative of a "
"dependent variable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/variable.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.variable.VariableDot:4
msgid ""
"This node will be discretised by :class:`.Discretisation` and converted to "
"a :class:`pybamm.StateVectorDot` node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/variable.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.variable.VariableDot:7
msgid "name of the node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/variable.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.variable.VariableDot:9
msgid "list of domains that this variable is valid over"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/variable.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.variable.VariableDot:23
msgid ""
"Physical bounds on the variable. Included for compatibility with "
"`VariableBase`, but ignored."
msgstr ""

